{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>והשתיה.</b> On the pattern of כח, regarding eating. For the dagesh of the yod is because of the absorbed yod that stands in place of the heh of the root." "<b>כדת</b> Like a statute, and it is feminine, joined to masculine [forms], like 'women and concubines'." "<b>אונס.</b> Compelling, close in meaning to 'and every secret is not compelled for you' (Daniel 2:23 in Aramaic)." "<b>רב ביתו.</b> Great, like 'and the great ones of the king'."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "The syntactic connection between כח and the eating reference is unclear in the source; rendered hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:38.334950504Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}